WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.200
Good morning, Hank, it's Tuesday.

00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:03.200
So I am very nearly 40,

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.740
which as it happens, means that I'm almost exactly

00:00:05.920 --> 00:00:08.980
twice as old as the median VlogBrothers viewer.

00:00:08.980 --> 00:00:12.040
When I was their age, half my life ago, I was a sophomore in college.

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:15.560
I had just fallen in love for the first time. I was taking my first creative writing class.

00:00:15.560 --> 00:00:17.300
I looked approximately like this:

00:00:17.300 --> 00:00:20.860
Of course, my life was very different then, and the world was different then too.

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:22.420
Specifically, it was worse.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:23.380
That year 1998

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:26.180
More than 10 million children under the age of 5 died.

00:00:26.180 --> 00:00:29.920
over 50% of kids in low income countries weren't vaccinated

00:00:29.920 --> 00:00:32.400
and 30% of all humans lived in absolute poverty

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:35.520
meaning that they survived on less than $2 a day

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:36.020
in current US Dollars.

00:00:36.020 --> 00:00:38.780
Today 80% of kids in low income countries are vaccinated

00:00:38.780 --> 00:00:41.180
Fewer than 10% of people on earth live in absolute poverty

00:00:41.180 --> 00:00:44.320
and this year fewer than 6 million children will die

00:00:44.320 --> 00:00:49.080
Child mortality isn't just falling, the rate it's falling has been accelerating for 2 decades

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:51.480
and after very slow progress for most of the 20th century

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:53.200
and for that matter all of human history

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:56.500
the cycle of poverty is suddenly breaking worldwide

00:00:56.760 --> 00:00:58.760
How did that happen and whats left to be done?

00:00:58.760 --> 00:01:01.040
well every year Melinda and Bill Gates

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:02.780
release there annual letter on those topics

00:01:02.780 --> 00:01:04.620
And for me it's kinda required reading every year

00:01:04.620 --> 00:01:07.120
Because like the news can tell me what happened yesterday

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.720
but reading the Gate's letter allows me to zoom out

00:01:09.820 --> 00:01:11.940
a little and think about what's happening

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:13.120
in the larger human story over time

00:01:13.560 --> 00:01:15.520
this years letter is written to Warren Buffet

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.120
Another Billionaire who's pledged almost all his wealth to charity

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:19.440
but it begins by pointing out

00:01:19.440 --> 00:01:21.420
that most money for global health initiatives

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.720
comes not from private individuals but from governments

00:01:24.720 --> 00:01:28.020
here in the US about $32 billion went to foreign aid last year

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.580
which is less than 1% of the federal governments budget

00:01:30.580 --> 00:01:31.800
but it still goes a long way

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:34.500
and I know foreign aid has a reputation for not working

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:36.600
but in fact it is extremely effective

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:39.760
and I also strongly believe that it's in our national interest

00:01:39.760 --> 00:01:41.740
like poverty and poor health are associated

00:01:41.740 --> 00:01:43.260
with an increased risk for conflict

00:01:43.260 --> 00:01:45.780
and also microbes are not aware of national borders

00:01:45.780 --> 00:01:47.800
so better healthcare systems around the world

00:01:47.800 --> 00:01:49.580
mean less disease risk for all of us

00:01:49.580 --> 00:01:52.300
ok. so as brilliantly explained in this video by in-a-nutshell

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:54.820
we know that when child mortality goes down

00:01:54.820 --> 00:01:56.720
families chose to have fewer children

00:01:56.720 --> 00:01:59.160
which ultimately slows population growth

00:01:59.160 --> 00:02:01.340
it also means that kids on average will be healthier

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.700
and more likely to go to school

00:02:02.700 --> 00:02:04.580
that there parents will be more likely to work

00:02:04.580 --> 00:02:06.500
Because they won't have to be home with sick kids

00:02:06.500 --> 00:02:08.860
so reducing child mortality has huge benefits

00:02:08.860 --> 00:02:11.760
not just for individual families but for entire social orders

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:12.620
as bill says:

00:02:15.860 --> 00:02:17.680
for one thing its often inexpensive

00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:19.620
like many vaccines cost less than a dollar

00:02:19.620 --> 00:02:23.720
and vaccination is the number 1 reason child mortality declined so much

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:28.360
but still most children who die do so only because they were born poor

00:02:28.560 --> 00:02:30.080
that is not acceptable

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:32.560
and also we don't have to accept it

00:02:32.560 --> 00:02:35.120
we need to continue to close the gap between rich and poor countries

00:02:35.120 --> 00:02:36.480
when it comes to vaccination

00:02:36.480 --> 00:02:37.920
we need to improve healthcare for infants

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:41.680
45% of child mortality now occurs within the first month of life

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:43.460
and we need to improve nutrition

00:02:43.460 --> 00:02:45.240
not just preventing starvation

00:02:45.240 --> 00:02:47.040
but ensuring that kids get all

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:48.380
the nutrients they need

00:02:48.380 --> 00:02:49.220
thats a really big deal

00:02:49.440 --> 00:02:50.480
as Bill puts it:

00:02:53.480 --> 00:02:55.180
because malnutrition can stunt not just

00:02:55.180 --> 00:02:57.460
physical growth but also cognitive development

00:02:57.460 --> 00:02:59.520
which jusy compounds the disadvantages

00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:01.300
that the poorest kids in the world face

00:03:01.300 --> 00:03:02.900
this year's Gates letter also focuses on

00:03:02.900 --> 00:03:04.280
access to contraception

00:03:04.300 --> 00:03:05.420
Melinda writes:

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.300
and this is another place

00:03:15.300 --> 00:03:16.840
where whats good for indivuals families can also

00:03:16.840 --> 00:03:18.840
have really positive impacts on the community

00:03:18.840 --> 00:03:20.340
as Melinda points out:

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:26.560
Hank, 20 years from now

00:03:26.560 --> 00:03:28.420
when today's median vlogbrothers viewer

00:03:28.420 --> 00:03:29.800
is as old as I am now

00:03:29.800 --> 00:03:31.580
it is genuinely possible that

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:32.940
both absolute poverty

00:03:32.940 --> 00:03:36.220
and child mortality will be rare everywhere on earth

00:03:36.220 --> 00:03:37.800
and I really belive that as a species

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.880
our sucess is best judged

00:03:39.880 --> 00:03:41.280
not by how the richest

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:42.920
or the best connected amoung us live

00:03:42.920 --> 00:03:46.100
but how the poor and the oppressed and the vulnerable live

00:03:46.100 --> 00:03:48.220
and I know that it may feel like absolute poverty

00:03:48.220 --> 00:03:50.240
and child mortality are beyond our control

00:03:50.240 --> 00:03:52.480
that only the Gateses and the Buffets of the world

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.560
can move the needle

00:03:53.560 --> 00:03:55.160
but in reality it's up to all of us

00:03:55.160 --> 00:03:56.400
like when my kids get through

00:03:56.400 --> 00:03:58.200
a diarrheal illness with just Pedialyte

00:03:58.260 --> 00:04:00.420
and Advil it's up to me to remember

00:04:00.420 --> 00:04:03.220
and to prioritize the kids who die of the very same

00:04:03.220 --> 00:04:05.840
disease for want of rehydration solution

00:04:05.840 --> 00:04:07.460
when we vote, when we talk to our friends about

00:04:07.460 --> 00:04:08.400
what matters to us

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:10.820
when we choose who's lives to pay attention to

00:04:10.820 --> 00:04:13.640
we are deciding what our future will look like

00:04:13.640 --> 00:04:16.760
Hank you told me once that bad news usually happens all at once

00:04:16.760 --> 00:04:18.820
while good news usually happens slowly

00:04:18.820 --> 00:04:21.260
and that makes it hard to pay attention to the good news

00:04:21.260 --> 00:04:22.800
but we still need the good news

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:24.200
maybe now more than ever

00:04:24.200 --> 00:04:25.700
so I really hope you'll check out the Gates' letter

00:04:25.700 --> 00:04:26.760
in the doobly-do below

00:04:26.760 --> 00:04:28.600
it's honest and level-headed

00:04:28.600 --> 00:04:30.020
while still being optimistic

00:04:30.020 --> 00:04:32.080
which is what I want to be when I grow up

00:04:32.080 --> 00:04:33.480
Hank, I'll see you on friday

